Sval: the hidden window's History menu closes after session store fakes its opening

On macOS, SessionStoreInternal.maybeSaveClosedWindow dispatches a synthetic
popupshowing on the hidden window's History menu when the first window
closes, so its key shortcuts are set up. HistoryMenu opens its Places result
on popupshowing and closes it only on popuphidden, which never came, so the
view kept observing history with no popup built. Once the result was
invalidated (history cleared), every later visit's title change or move threw
"No DOM node set for aPlacesNode" from PlacesViewBase. A matching popuphidden
closes the result, as a real open and close would.

diff --git a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
index 14218bec44..ee556f32c3 100644
--- a/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs
@@ -2732,6 +2732,12 @@ var SessionStoreInternal = {
           let historyMenu = window.document.getElementById("history-menu");
           let evt = new window.CustomEvent("popupshowing", { bubbles: true });
           historyMenu.menupopup.dispatchEvent(evt);
+          // The menu never opened, so close what popupshowing opened: the
+          // history view would otherwise keep following a result whose
+          // popup it never builds.
+          historyMenu.menupopup.dispatchEvent(
+            new window.CustomEvent("popuphidden", { bubbles: true })
+          );
         }
       } else if (!shouldStore) {
         if (
